# Tracer: C* is the nonzero complex standard set.
#
# Before (did not work):
# have z C*
# z $in C
# z != 0
# Former behavior: line 1 failed to parse with `Unexpected end of tokens`.
#
# Now (verified):
have z C*
z $in C
z != 0
i $in C*
1 $in C*
not 0 $in C*
R* $subset C*
C* $subset C

forall a, b C*:
    a * b $in C*

# Current behavior: C* supplies complex membership and nonzeroness, and is
# closed under multiplication through the existing complex and nonzero rules.
#
# Boundary: `0 $in C*`, `C $subset C*`, and unconditional additive closure
# remain rejected by executable Rust regressions; `N*` remains unsupported
# because `N+` is the canonical nonzero natural carrier.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/02_builtin_math/complex_star_standard_set.lit
